  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>CENTCOM conducted its 11th consecutive night of strikes on Iranian territory on July 21, targeting military logistics and missile storage facilities in Isfahan, Chabahar, Konarak, and Bandar Abbas, according to the CENTCOM communiqué released July 21. No strikes were confirmed against power-generation or oil-refining infrastructure as of the communiqué's publication. Trump made a public statement on July 22 naming "nuclear sites" as a future target category without confirmation of a formal targeting order from the Pentagon. → supports <span class="cite">N1</span> without move</p>

      <p>Rubio stated on July 20 that Iran had "effectively killed" the Islamabad MOU — a judgment backed by three separate Iranian attacks on commercial vessels in the Strait of Hormuz during July and Iran's continued withdrawal of IRGC-N patrol boats from demining coordination channels established under the MOU. The NBC News Hormuz tracker recorded 14 transits (9 outbound, 5 inbound) on July 19-20 against a pre-war baseline of 88+ per day; the 7-day rolling average remained below 15 for the full July 15-21 window. → moved <span class="cite">N2</span>, <span class="cite">N4</span></p>

      <p>Houthi forces declared a maritime blockade against Saudi Arabia on July 20, citing Saudi airstrikes on Sanaa airport and the naval blockade of Yemeni ports. Al-Bukhaiti announced the blockade via Telegram and X, naming "all Saudi oil tankers and energy export terminals" as target categories. Lloyd's List Intelligence and MarineTraffic both recorded tanker avoidance of Red Sea routes bound for Yanbu and Ras Tanura in the 48 hours following the declaration. → supports <span class="cite">N3</span> without move</p>

      <p>The Knesset voted formally for dissolution on July 17, two days after the EOD July 15 deadline in F6's resolution criteria, fixing the election for October 27, 2026. Channel 13's July 22 poll placed BeYachad at 23 seats vs Likud 22 — the first TIER1-confirmed poll since coalition collapse showing Bennett ahead of Netanyahu at the party level. Netanyahu remains caretaker PM under Israeli law pending the October 27 election. → moved <span class="cite">N5</span></p>

      <p>The Islamabad MOU, signed June 14 and the basis for F1 and F2's RESOLVED-YES outcomes, is now a closed historical event with no operative diplomatic framework in its place. Rubio's July 20 declaration confirms this status for official US government purposes. No replacement negotiating format, named mediator engagement, or confirmed meeting date between US and Iranian principals has been announced as of July 22. → supports <span class="cite">N2</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
