      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (35%):</strong> Driven by N1 (35% US energy-infrastructure strikes within 72h) and N3 (55% Houthi kinetic attack on Saudi oil before August 5); either event alone crosses a new threshold, while both together constitute a multi-front expansion of the conflict.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (55%):</strong> Active combat at current intensity without new threshold crossings — the dominant scenario given N2 (ceasefire, 15%) and N4 (Hormuz 15 transits/day, 10%) together yield a de-escalation ceiling of approximately 10%, leaving a 55% residual for sustained war at current tempo.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (10%):</strong> Conditioned on N2 (new ceasefire, 15%) and N4 (Hormuz partial opening, 10%) occurring jointly; joint probability is approximately 0.10–0.15 given N4's near-total dependency on a prior ceasefire, rounded to 10%.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Tasnim framed the 11 consecutive nights of US airstrikes as "Zionist-American terrorism against the Islamic Ummah" and attributed civilian casualties to "American war crimes against the Iranian nation." IRIB broadcast footage from Bandar Abbas and Konarak described as "martyrs' funerals," with anchors emphasizing IRGC steadfastness and popular resistance without acknowledging military losses or infrastructure damage assessed from satellite imagery. Kayhan's editorial board called for "retribution that breaks the aggressor's back" without specifying timeline or mechanism. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Mojtaba Khamenei remained absent from IRIB broadcasts through July 22 — absent during both the state funeral period July 4-9 and the active US military campaign. IRNA carried no statements attributed directly to the Supreme Leader beyond previously distributed written communiqués. The sustained absence from live broadcast across all state media platforms is the pattern tracked in <span class="cite">N6</span>; NCRI-affiliated sources reported domestic resistance activity in at least six provinces with no Supreme Leader response. → supports <span class="cite">N6</span> without move</p>

      <p>NCRI-documented reports from July 14-21 described power outages in Khuzestan, Isfahan, Fars, Hormozgan, Bushehr, and Razavi Khorasan provinces, attributed by residents to grid stress and suspected targeted degradation. IRNA attributed the outages to seasonal peak demand without citing external causes. None of the outages were confirmed as strike-related by TIER1 sources as of July 22; the absence of CENTCOM confirmation is the basis for N1's current NOT_OBSERVED status on the relevant indicator. → supports <span class="cite">N1</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

